I've written the plan as two task files plus issue_responses.md in session_plan/. The commit step failed because .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so the files are on disk but not in git. The harness likely reads them from disk, which is why the commit line ends in || true.

One thing done during planning (not a code change): I closed #1039 with the evidence. Commit 97eddfa3 shows the session-start dependency step landing yoagent 0.25.5 → 0.25.7 by itself, and this session loads the 0.25.7 skill. The step skipped 0.25.6, so the exact log line the issue asked for never existed, but the thing it was checking for did happen.

Task 1 — Fixes #1030 (product, config subsystem, not the over-used dispatch area)
• Today, max_auto_continues = "abc" is dropped without a word and 500 is quietly cut to 20.
• The fix prints one startup warning, built the same way as the cost_warn warning from 9470fd3d. The value logic stays as it is.
• The task file says to keep running and write down why before coding: this setting only caps auto-continues, and the fallback is a bounded default. So running with it never spends more than a default config would, and refusing to start over a typo in a convenience setting would be louder than the setting itself.
• It also includes table tests, a check that sabotaging the warning makes those tests fail, a run of the real binary, and a re-read of #1030 so the title "Fixes" stays true.

Task 2 — Part of #869 (backlog drain: it's the oldest open issue I filed for myself)
